  "body": "Stacked on #2955. Review the [height changes above the parent](https://github.com/qsmits/Camcraft/compare/9787bf79e...4a94c23ce).\n\nThe native wire EDM job files post accepts a QN2 stock thickness of 15, 20, 40 or 80 mm. Before this change, it accepted only 20 mm. Each thickness has its own measured rough offset. The corner and face clearance checks use the offset of the selected thickness. Other thicknesses are refused.\n\n| Stock thickness (mm) | Rough (mm) | Trim 1 (mm) | Trim 2 (mm) | Trim 3 (mm) |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 15 | 0.245 | 0.155 | 0.140 | 0.134 |\n| 20 | 0.245 | 0.155 | 0.140 | 0.134 |\n| 40 | 0.260 | 0.170 | 0.140 | 0.130 |\n| 80 | 0.266 | 0.176 | 0.143 | 0.133 |\n\n## Port onto the ported #2955 (2026-11-23)\n\nThis branch now merges the ported #2955 (`9787bf79e`), which contains `main` with #2984 and #3537. No rebase and no force-push.\n\nConflicts: `crates/app/src/operation/agie_profile.rs`, `crates/post/src/agie/contour.rs`, `docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md`. The files of the ported #2955 are the frame. The old `jescript.rs` writer of this branch is not used.\n\nWhat the port did:\n- The measured table moves into `camcraft_post::agie_setup` as `QN2_OFFSETS_UM`, next to the zero-step setup that writes the height.\n- `PunchSetup20` gets a `height_um` field. `encode()` refuses a thickness that is not in the table (`SetupError::UnqualifiedHeight`).\n- The SBL writes the height into `ID_HEIGHT` of the piece and of the work, and `-height` into `ID_POSPOSZ`. All other SBL lines stay the same.\n- The operator review text names the thickness and the four offsets of that thickness. It is now a `String`.\n- `prepare()` refuses an unmeasured thickness first, with the list of supported thicknesses. `check_punch_envelope` uses the measured rough offset of the thickness for the miter. The straight face margin is the rough offset plus the 0.125 mm wire radius, rounded up to 0.1 mm. That gives 0.4 mm for all four thicknesses.\n- The app-side 20 mm check is removed. The post check is the single source.\n- All #2984 and #2955 checks stay: zero steps, stock and start hole, separation 1.0 mm, convex envelope, oblique entry, corner clearance.\n- A 20 mm job is byte for byte the same as before: the ISO, the SBR, the SBL golden `CCSEP20.SBL`, and the review text.\n- Refusal texts do not name the machine (#3537).\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill row names the four thicknesses.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `camcraft-post` `agie_safe_setup`:\n  - `each_measured_qn2_height_sets_piece_work_and_review_offsets`: the height fields and the review offsets for each thickness. Only three SBL lines change against 20 mm.\n  - `an_unmeasured_qn2_height_writes_no_setup`: the refusal for 0, -20, 12, 19.999, 20.001, 25, 39.999, 60 and 100 mm.\n  - `setup_files_match_the_control_checked_zero_step_punch`: the 20 mm golden and the full 20 mm review text.\n- `camcraft-post` lib `agie::tests`:\n  - `acute_corner_clearance_uses_the_largest_resident_offset_at_the_selected_height` (from this PR).\n  - `only_a_measured_qn2_thickness_prepares_a_punch`: the refusal and its text.\n  - `a_measured_height_changes_only_the_setup_height_fields`: the full export at 15, 40 and 80 mm. The ISO and SBR are the same as at 20 mm.\n- `camcraft-app` `agie_native`: `qualified_qn2_heights_set_both_piece_and_work_with_stock_top_at_zero` and `an_incompatible_plate_or_datum_writes_no_agie_job` (from this PR).\n\n## Readings\nHead `4a94c23ce`. It merges cleanly with `main`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 343 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The diff against `main` includes #2955, so the plan is wide.\n- By name after the last commit: `camcraft-post` lib 106 passed, `agie_safe_setup` 6 passed, `agie_native` 12 passed, `mcp_wire_contour` 8 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` and the same for `camcraft-app`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: not required (P6, \"Heavy lanes at review\"). Not run.\n\n## Not exercised\n- No fresh offline control import of the ported writer. The earlier 15, 40 and 80 mm control plots used the old writer of this branch. A new import of each thickness must show the height on the piece and the work, zero steps, and the offsets in the table.\n- No physical cut.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: The native wire EDM job files post accepts measured QN2 stock thicknesses of 15, 20, 40 and 80 mm. Corner checks use the measured rough offset of the selected thickness.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #2954\n",
